  {
   "id": "aldo.buried",
   "once": true,
   "when": {
    "fact": "aldo.buried",
    "eq": true
   },
   "effect": [],
   "report": "They buried Aldo in the Watch's corner of the yard. Holloway read the words himself and got two of them wrong, and nobody corrected him. His wife is coming up from Low Kiln. Somebody will have to tell her about the leg."
  },
  {
   "id": "caravan.bodies",
   "once": true,
   "when": {
    "all": [
     {
      "fact": "caravan.bodies",
      "eq": true
     },
     {
      "not": {
       "history": "burned_roost"
      }
     }
    ]
   },
   "effect": [],
   "report": "Holloway's men brought the teamsters back from the ravine on a cart, under sacking. There were three. Harlan walked behind it all the way to the shrine, and when Chid lifted the sacking Harlan made a sound nobody on the square will forget."
  },
  {
   "id": "roost.ash",
   "once": true,
   "when": {
    "history": "burned_roost"
   },
   "effect": [],
   "report": "Smoke from the ravine all night, and the smell came over the wall with it. Rook burned rosemary in every room. Harlan has nailed his shutters closed from the inside."
  },
  {
   "id": "dig.burned",
   "once": true,
   "when": {
    "fact": "dig.pump",
    "eq": "blown"
   },
   "effect": [],
   "report": "The Watch says the lamplings were carrying their own out of the hillside all night: small, and burned, some still holding their lamps lit. One of them sat by the pile and counted them. It got to forty and started again."
  },
  {
   "id": "jory.nights",
   "once": true,
   "when": {
    "history": "freed_teamsters"
   },
   "effect": [],
   "report": "Jory Coyle woke the inn twice in the night, shouting for a man called Ewan. Rook sat with him until it was light. Ewan was in the fourth cage, he says. There isn't a fourth cage any more."
  },
  {
   "id": "shrine.bell",
   "once": true,
   "when": {
    "fact": "shrine.lit",
    "eq": true
   },
   "effect": [],
   "report": "Chid rang the shrine bell at first light, for the first time anyone can remember. Half the town came out thinking it was a fire. The other half came out because it wasn't."
  },
  {
   "id": "pelts.stacked",
   "once": true,
   "when": {
    "history": "wolf_slaughter"
   },
   "effect": [],
   "report": "Brannoc's yard is stacked with pelts to the eaves, and the flies have found it. Maeca walked past it this morning and did not look."
  },
  {
   "id": "nell.burial",
   "once": true,
   "when": {
    "any": [
     {
      "fact": "nell.told",
      "eq": "gone"
     },
     {
      "fact": "nell.told",
      "eq": "risen"
     }
    ]
   },
   "effect": {
    "set": {
     "nell.buried": true
    }
   },
   "report": "Brannoc banked his forge at noon yesterday and took a handcart down the Low Ford road, with a blanket and a spade. He was back before the gate shut, with something under his apron in the cart, and Chid walked out past the guards to meet him. They buried her at first light behind the shrine, next to the old captain. Nobody was asked to come, and half the town did."
  },
  {
   "id": "nell.asking",
   "once": true,
   "when": {
    "fact": "nell.asking",
    "eq": true
   },
   "effect": [],
   "report": "Brannoc stopped a pedlar off the south road at the gate yesterday, and asked him something. The pedlar shook his head. Brannoc asked the next one too."
  },
  {
   "id": "jory.words",
   "once": true,
   "when": {
    "fact": "jory.knows_be",
    "eq": true
   },
   "effect": [],
   "report": "Jory Coyle and his uncle had words in the yard before it was light. Jory did the shouting. Harlan didn't say anything at all, and then he opened the shop as usual."
  },
  {
   "id": "pell.taken",
   "once": true,
   "when": {
    "fact": "pell.fate",
    "eq": "taken"
   },
   "effect": [],
   "report": "Pell Varrow's door stood open at first light, the lock not forced. His bed had been slept in. There was a red thread caught on the hinge, and a cart went out of the east gate before cockcrow. Vonnra's lamp was lit in the toll tower all night; nobody has asked her what went through."
  },
  {
   "id": "pell.ran",
   "once": true,
   "when": {
    "fact": "pell.fate",
    "eq": "ran"
   },
   "effect": [],
   "report": "Pell Varrow left before dawn on a fast horse, with two satchels and none of his furniture. Three men in red came over the wall an hour after, kicked his door in, and found his ledgers gone with him."
  },
  {
   "id": "crates.harlan",
   "once": true,
   "when": {
    "fact": "be.crates",
    "eq": "harlan"
   },
   "effect": [],
   "report": "Two of Harlan's teamsters took an empty wagon out of the east gate at first light, with the Coyle purse. They came back after dark with the wagon full and covered, and wouldn't say from where. Harlan unloaded it himself."
  },
  {
   "id": "holloway.corran",
   "once": true,
   "when": {
    "fact": "holloway.post_told",
    "eq": true
   },
   "effect": [],
   "report": "Two of the Watch went down the Low Ford road at first light with a handcart and a spade, and came back at dusk with the cart covered. Holloway met them at the gate and walked beside it to the Watch's corner of the yard."
  },
  {
